PATCH 602: the render-phase byte DGROUP:0x1548 is a byte.

board:0017 / board:0023.  Every one of the 46 accesses in the image is a byte access -- `mov al,
[0x1548]`, `cmpb`, `movb`, `orb $0x80` (0x22bd, 0x22dd, 0x2315, 0x23d1, 0x494d, ..., 0x1a8d7); the
word beside it, 0x1549, is the viewport kind (0x1c cockpit / 0x20 map / 0x22 external) the object
pass c4df selects its method table by.  Ghidra typed DAT_1000_d548 as a word: every `= 0/1/2/3`
store zeroed the viewport byte and every `== 0` test read it.  The M1 cockpit's windshield method
795c survived by accident (its map sibling's word store zeroed 0x1549 for it); after the switch to
the Bradley the map's method 842d stores its byte correctly, so 0x1549 stayed 0x20, 8390's word
test never saw zero, and the windshield never started another phase sequence: no object pass, no
shell drawn, the port's 3D view frozen behind the Bradley's instruments for the rest of the mission
(the seeded replay's shell-draw lists, patch 600, empty from step 2682).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -2679,7 +2679,7 @@
 #define DAT_1000_c790 (*(undefined2 *)(g_mem+0x1c790))
 #define DAT_1000_c794 (*(undefined2 *)(g_mem+0x1c794))
 #define DAT_1000_cf69 (*(undefined2 *)(g_mem+0x1cf69))
-#define DAT_1000_d548 (*(undefined2 *)(g_mem+0x1d548))
